PRECISION A GAS MASS WOULD NEED (arithmetic on CFG273's own columns; no s* computed)
  separation of the rival from FLAT in log a0 = log10 E(z), E = sqrt(Om (1+z)^3 + 1 - Om), Om 0.30 / 0.315 (PAPER38's range);
  a COMMON-MODE baryon-calibration error sigma_cal moves log s* by |lever| sigma_cal and does not average down, so a k-sigma
  separation needs sigma_cal <= log10 E / (k |lever|). lever = CFG273's d log10 s*/d(baryon dex) at STARS-ONLY baryons;
  adding the gas FLAT needs raises y and |lever| (toward the Newtonian side), so these are upper bounds on sigma_cal.
